        "The governance challenge in HD-55 is specific: the relevant minority constituency is the Hispanic agricultural and industrial workforce, whose needs center on job quality, workplace conditions, housing affordability, and access to Spanish-language services rather than tribal sovereignty and economic development. This requires a different constituent engagement approach than most rural Oklahoma districts — one oriented toward workforce and economic mobility rather than tribal partnership. A representative who actively serves the 13.1% Hispanic community through specific, bilingual constituent engagement and who addresses the working-class economic conditions of a $55K community is building the full-constituency record that distinguishes genuine representation from uncontested incumbency."
