        "The roughly 11% of residents not accounted for by the four reported demographic categories are primarily AIAN — tribal citizens of nations with territory and citizenship in north-central Oklahoma whose economic development interests and state-tribal relationship expectations are live governance questions, not ceremonial acknowledgments. Dick Lowe's uncontested 2024 result reflects the absence of organized opposition, not the absence of constituent need. Rural healthcare access, agricultural infrastructure, and the conditions that sustain the energy economy are the practical concerns that cut across partisan lines and demand active legislative engagement — not the comfortable assumption that an unopposed seat is a managed seat."
