        "The demographic diversity of HD-67 is exceptional for this geographic sequence: 8.74% Hispanic, 7.71% Black, and 6.93% Asian together with a ~11% AIAN gap mean that roughly 35% of the district's residents are from communities that often find their specific interests inadequately represented in a generic partisan majority. At a 51-49 margin, each of these communities is potentially swing-deciding — a candidate who maintains authentic relationships with the Black, Hispanic, Asian, and Native American constituencies while serving the professional majority that comprises the largest cohort will find the full-constituency approach is also the only electoral approach that sustains a one-point lead. No candidate can afford to govern for 65% of the district and win 51% of the votes here over multiple cycles."
