        "The 33.96% Hispanic community in HD-77 has specific material needs that require legislative specificity — workforce access, language services, housing stability, and the economic infrastructure of a working-class immigrant community navigating Oklahoma's labor and housing markets. At 32.7 median age, this is a young district whose residents are in their prime family-formation and career-building years, when access to affordable housing and quality employment are most consequential. A representative who delivers tangible improvements in renter protections, healthcare access, and language-accessible government services converts an unopposed seat into a genuinely accountable one. One who coasts on the partisan margin will find the constituency's urgency eventually converted into disengagement or a primary challenge from within."
