        "The 12.98% Black community is the defining swing constituency in HD-83. In a 55-45 seat, this community's turnout and candidate preference are among the most direct determinants of the electoral outcome — and a 13% Black community in an $83.6K income district includes both professional families with high governance expectations and working-class households with material needs around economic access, public safety, and community investment. The additional 6.82% Hispanic and 4.16% Asian communities, plus the ~10.7% AIAN gap, mean that more than a third of the district is non-White — a minority coalition whose combined weight makes this seat's Republican margin genuinely vulnerable in the absence of active, authentic constituent engagement."
