        { name: "Treating Tribal Sovereignty as a Peripheral or Special-Interest Issue", tag: "avoid", why: "In a near-majority AIAN district, tribal sovereignty, Indian Health Service access, tribal economic development, and the state-tribal relationship are mainstream governance priorities — not niche accommodations for a special interest. A legislator who positions these issues as secondary is defining the primary constituency to exclude nearly half the district's population. In central Oklahoma tribal territory, the tribal nations operating here are government-to-government partners with the state, not interest groups competing with other constituents for a legislator's attention." }
